{{- /*
.chezmoiremove — paths to delete from $HOME on each `chezmoi apply`.
Templated; re-evaluated every apply (idempotent — chezmoi only acts
when the path actually exists). One pattern per line.

Currently used to clean up the zsh-side copies of files that were
moved into the shared dot_config/shell/ POSIX layer (see commit
9bb56c2 "shell: extract POSIX layer..." 2026-05). Without this, the
orphan ~/.config/zsh/ files would still get sourced by
load_modular_dir and double-load PATH/env on every shell start.

Pruning policy: leave entries forever unless the file grows large
(>50 lines). `stat()` on each non-existent path is a few µs per
apply — negligible cost vs the safety of cleaning up any host that
hasn't applied since the migration commit. After ~6-12 months on
the fleet, individual entries can be pruned in a follow-up commit
if the maintainer is confident every host has applied at least
once. Tracked as a [P3/S] follow-up in TODO.md; not urgent.
*/ -}}
